---
description: Best practices for React 19.1 (with Next.js 15)
globs: */src/app/**/*.tsx,*/src/app/**/*.ts,*/app/**/*.tsx,*/app/**/*.ts,*/src/components/**/*.tsx,*/src/components/**/*.ts,*/components/**/*.tsx,*/components/**/*.ts,*/src/hooks/**/*.ts,*/src/hooks/**/*.tsx,*/src/app/**/*.js,*/src/app/**/*.jsx,*/app/**/*.js,*/app/**/*.jsx,*/src/components/**/*.js,*/src/components/**/*.jsx,*/components/**/*.js,*/components/**/*.jsx
---

- Prefer function components and hooks; avoid legacy lifecycles.
- Use Actions/form actions patterns where applicable (framework-integrated).
- Keep client component state minimal; lift server data fetching to server components.
- Optimize re-renders with memoization (React.memo/useMemo/useCallback) only when measured.
- Use Suspense boundaries for streaming/async UI.
- Strictly type props and component contracts with TS 5.9.

